Ticket **#4471** was opened for day-first tenants whose dates land on the wrong day. The desk
merged **412** reports into it and marked the ticket **known** as one parser bug. The export
shows **two** causes in that pile, not one.

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

<Callout>
The ticket’s owner cause is <code>parser</code> (379 reports). **33** reports are
<code>hint</code>: booking-v3 shows an MM/DD hint while the tenant locale is day-first, so people
type month-first and the form parses day-first. That is a different fix from the shared parser
reading every date month-first.
</Callout>

## What to file

| cause | reports | belongs on #4471? |
| --- | ---: | --- |
| `parser` | 379 | yes — shared parser reads month first |
| `hint` | 33 | no — split to its own ticket |

Intake tagged many `hint` reports as `parser` because the subject lines match #4471. Group by
cause (`causes.ts` + tenant locale and form), not by subject alone.

